{% comment %}
Prompt C's user message, in three parts.

The goal as written, one line per step: the step (its comments above it, its indentation kept), then
after `=> decider:` what the decider listed for it (step.Pick.Listed: each action with its score and
mark), then after `=> formal:` the starting line (step.Pick.Formal) when anything is certain.

Types — the literal types first (text, number, bool, list, dict), then every type a listed action's
properties use, in the order the goal first reaches them: the type's Description, a choice's options,
its Example, whichever it has.

Then every listed action ONCE (goal.call too when a listed action holds actions): its signature, the
first line of its description, its notes (their headings one level down).

The eval's shape (tools/decider/prompt_c.py user_message_c); a twin test holds the two equal.
Needs: goal (its steps' Pick taken), modules (%!app.module.list%).
{% endcomment %}Goal, as written:
  {{ goal.Name }}
{%- assign shown = "|" -%}
{%- for s in goal.Step -%}
{%- capture indent -%}{% if s.Indent > 0 %}{% for k in (1..s.Indent) %}    {% endfor %}{% endif %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign width = s.Index | append: "" | size | plus: 3 -%}
{%- capture pad -%}{% for k in (1..width) %} {% endfor %}{{ indent }}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if s.Comment -%}
{%- assign commentLines = s.Comment | split: "\n" -%}
{%- for c in commentLines %}
  {{ pad }}/ {{ c }}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif %}
  [{{ s.Index }}] {{ indent }}- {{ s.Text }} => decider: {% if s.Pick.Listed.size == 0 %}(nothing it is sure of){% endif -%}
{%- for l in s.Pick.Listed -%}
{{ l.Name }} {{ l.Shown }}{% case l.Mark %}{% when "Possible" %} (possible){% when "WriteTo" %} (write to){% when "Popular" %} (possible, popular){% endcase %}{% unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless %}
{%- assign mark = "|" | append: l.Name | append: "|" -%}
{%- unless shown contains mark -%}{%- assign shown = shown | append: l.Name | append: "|" -%}{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if s.Pick.Formal %} => formal: {{ s.Pick.Formal }}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- comment %} goal.call's definition, when a listed action holds actions (an action property, a Recovery) {% endcomment -%}
